# Counter-instances (tasks.org, aida-referents-counter-instances, settled
# 2026-10-22).  gen presumes P of anybody; not_c refutes P c strictly.
# The refutation defeats the instance P c only: a's site P x under its
# binder x stays IN, x being any individual.  The closed universal a
# derives falls as one, through no, which refutes it at an individual of
# its own choice: the witness scaffold tries c, about which P c is stated.
lk.
pipeline unfolded.
declare iota : type.
declare c : iota.
declare P : iota -> bool.
deny not_pc : (P [c]).
argument gen : P [?z].
by default.
dixi.
argument a : (forall x:iota, P [x]).
elim x.
next.
dixi.
counterargument not_c : P [c].
moxia not_pc.
dixi.
counterargument no : [?c:iota] (forall x:iota, P [x]).
elim [?c].
next.
dixi.
